1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,808
This is Mosaic Vault, a modular lending layer we built on Mezo testnet.

2
00:00:04,858 --> 00:00:07,757
Deposit Bitcoin, or another supported asset,

3
00:00:07,807 --> 00:00:10,840
and borrow MUSD without selling what you hold.

4
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:14,214
Every asset gets its own isolated vault.

5
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:17,122
If something goes wrong with one collateral type,

6
00:00:17,172 --> 00:00:20,980
the damage stays with that asset and never spreads to the others.

7
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:26,311
The collateral page reads straight from the on-chain registry.

8
00:00:26,361 --> 00:00:31,690
Each asset has its own maximum loan-to-value, liquidation threshold, penalty,

9
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,647
borrow cap and exposure cap.

10
00:00:33,697 --> 00:00:37,629
Real testnet BTC is priced by Mezo's own BTC to USD feed,

11
00:00:37,679 --> 00:00:41,890
and the oracle adapter rejects any price that has gone stale.

12
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:47,358
Borrowed MUSD comes from a lending pool that liquidity providers fund.

13
00:00:47,408 --> 00:00:52,273
Mosaic never mints MUSD, and it never touches Mezo's native borrowing system.

14
00:00:52,323 --> 00:00:55,720
The numbers you see here are read live from the chain.

15
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:59,516
To use it, you connect with Mezo Passport.

16
00:00:59,566 --> 00:01:03,244
It supports Bitcoin wallets like Unisat, OKX and Xverse,

17
00:01:03,294 --> 00:01:05,640
as well as regular Ethereum wallets.

18
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:09,815
The protocol page shows exposure against every cap,

19
00:01:09,865 --> 00:01:11,745
how fresh each oracle price is,

20
00:01:11,795 --> 00:01:15,045
and a live scan for positions that can be liquidated.

21
00:01:15,095 --> 00:01:18,220
Managers can also pause the engine in an emergency.

22
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:23,157
Risk managers list new assets and tune their parameters here.

23
00:01:23,207 --> 00:01:25,739
Every change is an on-chain transaction,

24
00:01:25,789 --> 00:01:28,450
and each action is locked to its own role.

25
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,300
All of this is deployed on Mezo testnet.

26
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:38,073
We ran the full journey on-chain: fund the pool, deposit, borrow, add collateral,

27
00:01:38,123 --> 00:01:42,491
repay, withdraw, and finally a liquidation after a price drop.

28
00:01:42,541 --> 00:01:46,410
This is that liquidation, settled on the Mezo explorer.

29
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:52,628
We also borrowed against real testnet BTC, through Mezo's BTC token,

30
00:01:52,678 --> 00:01:55,390
then repaid and withdrew it in full.

31
00:01:56,440 --> 00:02:00,963
We ran a security review on the contracts and fixed the critical findings,

32
00:02:01,013 --> 00:02:05,599
so a liquidation can never write off debt that the collateral still covers.

33
00:02:05,649 --> 00:02:10,604
Every contract is linked right here in the footer. Mosaic Vault: more collateral,

34
00:02:10,654 --> 00:02:13,880
and more access to Bitcoin-backed liquidity, on Mezo.
